# PowerShell Safety Rules

## Version
- ALWAYS use pwsh 7 (PowerShell 7.6.6, Microsoft Store).
- NEVER use Windows PowerShell 5.1 (`powershell.exe`) — mangles `$_`, breaks JSON argv.

## Script Patterns
- For >1 line, write to `.ps1` file and execute with `pwsh -File script.ps1`.
- Never inline `{ ... }` scriptblocks in `-Command` parameters.
- Never nest single quotes in inline strings.

## Non-Interactive Safety
- `agent-init.ps1` loads functions in non-interactive shells (early return pattern).
- PSReadLine and Terminal-Icons hang in non-interactive mode — the profile handles this.
- Detection: `[Console]::IsInputRedirected -or [Console]::IsOutputRedirected`.

## Encoding
- UTF-8 is set by `agent-init.ps1`. No additional encoding setup needed.
- For file output: `$PSDefaultParameterValues['Out-File:Encoding'] = 'utf8'` (already set).

## Common Pitfalls
| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
|---------|-------|-----|
| `ParserError` with `$_` | PS 5.1 parsing | Use pwsh 7 or script file |
| Profile hangs | PSReadLine in non-interactive | Early return pattern (already in profile) |
| `Get-AppxPackage` fails | Store version restriction | Use MSI version or skip Appx |
